From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:41:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: Share a file's delete disposition among its opens by
 that name.

On Windows the disposition belongs to the name ([MS-FSA] 2.1.5.15.3:
Open.Link.IsDeleted), so setting it through one handle marks the file
for deletion for all of them, and clearing it through another keeps the
file; Wine kept a flag on each fd and deleted the file at the close of
the one that had set it, whatever the others said since.  Clearing it
also takes back the delete left by an open for delete on close that has
been closed; removing the name at once (POSIX semantics) remains for the
close of the open that asked for it.

A name marked for deletion cannot be opened again (STATUS_DELETE_PENDING,
ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED to CreateFile), renamed or linked to, and a file with
no name left reports DeletePending.  One that is only marked still does
not: telling would take a server call on every FileStandardInformation
query, some four times what the query costs now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

